{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"INVESTIGATION (new session, independent verification + live experiments). All handoff data claims re-verified from the four traces; one NEW blocking discovery changes the actuator design.\n\nNEW FINDING — the shipped forced-landing primitive is broken at the provider layer (LIVE-proven on Bedrock us-east-1, haiku-4.5):\n- build_agent_kwargs rewrites toolsets to .filtered(run_step <= limit). When the filter trips AFTER any tool call, pydantic-ai omits tools/toolConfig from the next request while history still holds toolUse blocks. Bedrock Converse rejects this: ValidationException 400 'The toolConfig field must be defined when using toolUse and toolResult content blocks.' (exp_e, exp_f: rebar's exact filter shape -> ModelHTTPError 400, not a landing.)\n- Same class of failure on Anthropic direct (documented API constraint: tools must be defined when history contains tool_use); pydantic_ai bedrock.py maps tool_choice='none' to omitting toolConfig entirely -> same 400. There is NO pydantic-ai-native way to 'remove tools mid-run' that is protocol-safe on our two first-class providers.\n- CONSEQUENCE: completion_recovery's own evidence runs pass tool_step_limit=16 (completion_recovery.py:471, _EVIDENCE_TOOL_STEPS) — the shipped fallback carries the identical 400 grenade. Any evidence run reaching step 17 dies with a provider error, not a bound.\n- Why tests never caught it: test_agent_call_seam.py + test_runner_pydantic_budget.py drive the cutoff with FunctionModel, which happily accepts a tools-less request over a tool_use history. The provider protocol constraint is unrepresented offline.\n\nWORKING REPLACEMENT (LIVE-proven, exp_g + exp_h): synthetic tool-result steering. A WrapperToolset whose call_tool, once the detector trips, stops executing and returns a steering notice ('LOOP BREAKER ENGAGED... produce your final answer NOW') instead. Tools stay defined -> protocol always valid on both providers; no exception mid-run; the model lands naturally. exp_g: a deliberately tool-happy agent landed after 3 real + 7 steered calls. exp_h: the landing produced a VALID completion_verdict through rebar's own schema_directive + parse_structured (PromptedOutput path) — 4 real + 2 steered calls, parsed verdict OK. Also observed 10 tool calls in 2 requests (parallel calls), re-confirming request_limit alone cannot bound the tool-call kill path.\n\nROUTING TRAPS (proven against real rebar code, exp_c): (1) any new typed loop exception raised today is swept by interpret_failure's third branch into LLMUnavailableError — runaway reads as provider outage; a typed branch must precede the sweep. (2) UsageLimitExceeded -> LLMRunnerError, which CompletionAgentStep.run does NOT catch (only UnretryableOutputError + token-exhaustion text check) -> bounded recovery is unreachable on budget exhaustion (confirms fd84).\n\nDETECTOR (re-verified from all four traces): windowed distinct-ratio, window 24, trip <=0.50, order-insensitive — fires at calls 88/151/196 on the three pathological runs, never on the clean run (clean minimum w24 ratio 0.833, wide margin). Adjacency metric max_consecutive_repeat confirmed inverted (4-cycle scores 1; healthy run scores 5) — see 70bc.\n\nOSS RESEARCH: industry consensus is detect -> forced tool-free final answer (LangChain early_stopping_method=generate, smolagents provide_final_answer, CrewAI handle_max_iterations_exceeded, LangGraph remaining_steps, OpenAI Agents SDK RunErrorHandlers). pydantic-ai itself has NO graceful-landing support (issue #2605 open; tool_calls_limit/check_before_tool_call merged 2025-09 are hard-fail only). Synthetic tool-result steering is the protocol-safe variant for Anthropic/Bedrock.\n\nProposed architecture follows in next comment. Experiment scripts: /tmp/gate-experiments/exp_{a,c,d,e,f,g,h}*.py (this host)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785953314122820001,"uuid":"caa7b69b-27a9-4ce3-b685-f62b28e6491d"}